The values is a list of 1, 3, 2, 5, 3, -1, and 9.
The lefts is a list of 1, 3, 5, -1, -1, -1, and -1.
The rights is a list of 2, 4, 6, -1, -1, -1, and -1.
The queue is an empty list of whole numbers.
Place 0 into queue.
The head is 0.
The count is 1.
The remaining is 1.
The levelcount is 1.
The nextcount is 0.
The best is 0.
The answers is an empty list of whole numbers.
Repeat while head is less than count.
The node is item head of queue.
Add 1 to head.
If remaining is levelcount, set best to item node of values.
If remaining is not levelcount and item node of values is more than best, set best to item node of values.
If item node of lefts is at least 0, Place item node of lefts into queue, add 1 to count, add 1 to nextcount.
If item node of rights is at least 0, Place item node of rights into queue, add 1 to count, add 1 to nextcount.
Subtract 1 from remaining.
If remaining is 0, Place best into answers, set remaining to nextcount, set levelcount to nextcount, set nextcount to 0.

For each value in answers, show value.
